    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know it's a symptom or whatever but it doesn't feel like a symptom, it just feels like the truth. like the \"real world\" is just this loud, heavy, exhausting thing that i'm not actually a part of anymore. it's like i'm watching a movie of someone else's life and i'm just a spectator. it feels so much more peaceful to just... fade out. like if i stopped trying to be \"real\" maybe it wouldnt hurt so much to just disappear.",
